From 340c8894228735e3c9daad7126835b0f32a2c628 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pedrobartolini <pedrobartolini@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 22:54:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: bind every offered relay and answer probes only for
 them

Phones run client-side relay election shortly after accept and migrate
their media to the offered relay they measured closest (c2r_rtt in the
offer); a callee bound to a single relay goes deaf 5-8 comfort-noise
packets in, while WhatsApp Web callers never migrate - the exact
symptom of #21 and #22. Connect and allocate on every offered relay,
broadcast sends, merge receives behind an (ssrc, seq) replay filter
(a duplicate timestamp resets the playout buffer), and re-send each
relay its own allocate in the keepalive. relaylatency probes are now
answered only for relays present in the offer, so the election cannot
settle on the caller's own nearest edge, a relay the callee holds no
tokens for. Group calls keep the previous single-relay semantics.

Live-validated against Android consumer, Android Business, iPhone and
web callers; the live relay hop has no KAT vector, matching the
validation state of the existing relay code.

Source of truth: https://github.com/JotaDev66/WaCalls/blob/edeb31f0427aba896639db503153b777a405eccf/internal/voip/transport/sctprelay.go#L105-L127
Source of truth: https://github.com/JotaDev66/WaCalls/blob/edeb31f0427aba896639db503153b777a405eccf/internal/voip/transport/sctprelay.go#L345-L355
